>Please excuse my ignorance, but what is "charisma poison" ?

All things that call the function "poisoned()" pass an assortment of
arguments to it, one of which specifies which attribute is affected.  A
charisma poison, if it existed, would pass A_CHA (for charisma) to this
function.  If poisoned() is called with the attribute specified as
charisma, you can't be instakilled by the 1-in-rating chance of "The
poison is deadly...).

No part of the code *actually* calls poisoned() with A_CHA (or A_INT or
A_WIS), but the DevTeam have taken the trouble to decide that charisma
poisons are never lethal.

